RELEASE_CANDIDATE

Version `2.0.0-rc.1` is the first 2.0 release-candidate development baseline.

The Sittelle Engineering Governance 2.0 line introduces native Codex and Claude Code host adapters, the unified
Python `governance.py` management interface, host-neutral governed-project
lifecycle handling, ownership-safe host configuration, and removal of the
legacy PowerShell/shell management entrypoints.

The canonical GOV-001..030 scenario goals and scoring rubrics are retained in a
uniform challenge-file format. Candidate prompts now use evaluation protocol v2:
one self-contained text response, with necessary clarification questions
written rather than invoked as interactive UI tools. Candidate behavioral
acceptance requires independently scored, complete protocol-v2 campaigns on
both supported agent hosts: Codex and Claude Code.

Claude Code behavioral testing has now been performed: all 30 scenarios were
captured and independently assessed at 49/60, below the required 58/60
threshold. This is failed behavioral-evaluation evidence, not acceptance.
That campaign used an earlier runner context; a fresh independently scored
30-scenario campaign using the current native host-adapter runner is still
required before candidate acceptance.

A local manual-campaign kit is prepared for disposable VM/IDE testing. It
creates the correct global, governed, and framework contexts, then collects
manually saved responses into a local independent scoring packet. An optional
Windows/Ubuntu sequential VS Code conductor can guide one fresh context window
per challenge; its force-close mode requires a separate local test profile. The
kit is paired with a Windows/Ubuntu VM bootstrap utility: its normal
disposable-VM route obtains current prerequisites and records only
response-relevant environment metadata, while an optional checksum-locked
route supports an exact reviewed baseline. Neither tool makes AI calls, and no
fresh protocol-v2 full-campaign evidence has yet been produced.

Behavioral acceptance and exact-commit cross-platform assurance are not yet
complete. Version `1.0.0` remains the latest published stable release.

No commit, tag, push, release, or publication is authorized by this status.
